Usage: mailman create [OPTIONS] LISTNAME

  Create a mailing list.

  The 'fully qualified list name', i.e. the posting address of the mailing
  list is required.  It must be a valid email address and the domain must be
  registered with Mailman.  List names are forced to lower case.

Options:
  --language CODE                 Set the list's preferred language to CODE,
                                  which must be a registered two letter
                                  language code.
  -o, --owner OWNER               Specify a list owner email address.  If the
                                  address is not currently registered with
                                  Mailman, the address is registered and
                                  linked to a user. Mailman will send a
                                  confirmation message to the address, but it
                                  will also send a list creation notice to the
                                  address.  More than one owner can be
                                  specified.
  -n, --notify / -no-notify, -N   Notify the list owner by email that their
                                  mailing list has been created.
  -q, --quiet                     Print less output.
  -d, --domain / -D, --no-domain  Register the mailing list's domain if not
                                  yet registered.  This is the default
                                  behavior, but these options are provided for
                                  backward compatibility.  With -D do not
                                  register the mailing list's domain.
  -h, --help                      Show this message and exit.
